1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,290
Before you use any player-prop model, you
should be able to

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,200
answer a few basic questions.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,540
What exact line is it analyzing?

4
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:10,220
What evidence is behind the signal?

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:12,440
What changed since it was analyzed?

6
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:14,740
And what can the model not know?

7
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:18,080
That is what Propeller Picks is built for.

8
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:23,280
Propeller is an AI-assisted player-prop
research workspace for web and mobile.

9
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,160
It is not a sportsbook.

10
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,780
It does not take wagers, place entries,

11
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:31,850
or promise outcomes. Its job is to make
the evidence around

12
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:36,760
a specific player, stat, direction, and
line easier to inspect.

13
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,320
There are two related ways to use
Propeller.

14
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:45,210
The first is player-prop research: should
the available evidence lean More

15
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:47,360
or Less for this exact player line?

16
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:51,860
The second is fantasy research: what is a
reasonable floor,

17
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,790
point projection, and ceiling for an
eligible player in the current

18
00:00:55,800 --> 00:01:00,940
scoring context? They use different
outputs because they answer different
questions.

19
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,780
Start with the free Prop Analyzer.

20
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:07,060
Choose a sport, find an available player
line,

21
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,940
and open the prop you want to research.

22
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:13,750
The exact player, stat, direction, and
displayed line are the unit

23
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:17,480
of analysis. If the line moves, the
question changes.

24
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:23,150
A research result tied to 22.5 points is
not automatically the

25
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:26,050
same research result at 24.5.

26
00:01:26,060 --> 00:01:31,270
For the displayed line, Propeller
evaluates the sport-specific context that

27
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:35,230
is available and summarizes it as a
direction plus a 50-to-100

28
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:38,840
confidence score. Depending on the sport
and market,

29
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:43,150
that context can include recent
production, role and opportunity,

30
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:47,800
matchup, injuries and lineup effects,
market context,

31
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:52,140
and game environment. That is where the
agents come in.

32
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:56,130
An agent is not a generic chatbot and it
is not

33
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,100
a fixed vote in a simple poll.

34
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:03,120
In Propeller, agents are separate
sport-specific analysis signals.

35
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:06,320
Each one focuses on a different source of
context,

36
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:10,830
and the model combines the signals that
return usable evidence for

37
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,620
the player prop in front of you.

38
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,390
Take a basketball prop as an example.

39
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:19,580
The Minutes agent looks at playing-time
trajectory and blowout risk.

40
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:23,450
The Usage agent looks at the volume of
opportunity a player

41
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:24,720
is likely to have.

42
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:28,510
The Pace agent asks whether the game
environment creates more or

43
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:33,110
fewer possessions. The Injury agent looks
beyond one player’s status to

44
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,970
the downstream role changes that can
follow a scratch or lineup

45
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:41,360
change. And the Matchup agent adds
opponent and position context.

46
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:45,120
Market context is separate for a reason.

47
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:50,030
The No-Vig or market signal can compare
the implied probabilities available

48
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:53,440
across books after removing the bookmaker
margin.

49
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:57,140
If the market disagrees with a posted
player line,

50
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:59,500
that creates a research question.

51
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,500
It does not automatically prove that
either side is valuable.

52
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,870
Other agents can account for recent form,

53
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:10,480
hit-rate trends, rest, or sport-specific
conditions.

54
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:14,970
In baseball, the important evidence may
lean more heavily toward pitching

55
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:19,260
matchup, park, handedness, batting role,
and lineup context.

56
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:22,830
In football, it can be opportunity,
matchup,

57
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:27,190
and game environment. The right evidence
is not identical across every

58
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:31,410
sport or prop. That is also why Propeller
does not publish

59
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:35,850
one universal agent count or pretend every
agent always has the

60
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:40,680
same weight. Signal availability and
active weighting can vary by sport,

61
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:44,060
prop, model version, and production
calibration.

62
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:48,280
Only available signals contribute to the
directional score.

63
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:53,110
A missing input is a limitation to
disclose—not a neutral vote

64
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,860
that silently makes the model look more
certain.

65
00:03:56,320 --> 00:04:00,770
On both desktop and mobile, open the agent
breakdown before you

66
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:02,320
give a score too much meaning.

67
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:05,060
You should be able to see what supports
the direction,

68
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:08,970
what pushes back, and which part of the
research deserves another

69
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:12,740
look. Agreement can make a case easier to
understand.

70
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:17,810
Conflict can be just as valuable:
opportunity may support a side

71
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:20,760
while matchup or market context adds
caution.

72
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:23,460
Now read confidence correctly.

73
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:26,870
Start with the displayed direction: More
or Over,

74
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,060
or Less or Under.

75
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:31,030
Then read the score as the strength of the
model’s directional

76
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:33,080
signal for that exact line.

77
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:36,740
A higher number means stronger support for
the side shown,

78
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:38,380
based on the usable evidence.

79
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:41,870
It does not mean that side has the same
percentage chance

80
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:46,170
of winning. A confidence score of 72 is
not a 72

81
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:50,200
percent probability, a guarantee, or a
promise of profit.

82
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:54,420
The workflow is more important than any
single number.

83
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,120
Confirm the current line.

84
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:58,660
Read direction and confidence together.

85
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,360
Open the agent breakdown.

86
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:05,220
Check lineup news, player status,
freshness, and market movement.

87
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:10,030
Then decide whether the evidence is strong
enough to keep researching—or

88
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,300
whether passing is the smarter decision.

89
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:16,580
Propeller also has a distinct
fantasy-projections workflow.

90
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:22,600
The current public feature covers MLB
hitters under DraftKings MLB scoring.

91
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,860
Instead of returning an Over or Under
signal,

92
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:29,260
it produces a floor, a central point
projection,

93
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,660
and a ceiling for eligible hitters.

94
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:38,430
Technically, the central MLB fantasy
projection converts available current
hitter-stat

95
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:41,660
market components into DraftKings fantasy
points.

96
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:46,070
Recent form is used for scoring components
that do not have

97
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:51,390
current market coverage. Recent outcome
variation then widens the lower

98
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:54,240
and upper distances around the central
projection.

99
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:58,020
Those three numbers are scenarios, not
guarantees.

100
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,920
The point projection is the central
estimate.

101
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:05,950
The floor and ceiling are widened
P20-style and P80-style ranges,

102
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:10,130
so an actual fantasy result can finish
below the floor or

103
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:14,250
above the ceiling. The current public
feature does not publish pitcher

104
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:20,160
projections, non-MLB projections, lineup
optimization, salary optimization,

105
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:25,810
or contest-entry submission. It is
research input for daily fantasy,

106
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:31,030
player comparison, and sit/start
decisions—not an automated lineup

107
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:34,260
tool. Freshness matters here too.

108
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:38,790
The fantasy board shows its source-update
state so you can distinguish

109
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:42,760
current data from latest available or
unavailable data.

110
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:47,290
Late lineup news and role changes can
still alter the research

111
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:51,070
picture. And you should be able to inspect
the record behind

112
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:56,260
the product. Propeller publishes a public
historical Results archive with wins,

113
00:06:56,820 --> 00:07:00,800
losses, pushes, sport splits, and
confidence ranges.

114
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:07,270
As of July 22, 2026, it includes more than
2.18 million

115
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:12,820
raw graded analysis rows and a
293-thousand-entry public ledger.

116
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,440
Those numbers need context.

117
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:20,880
Historical rows can include repeated
snapshots and legacy retrospective data.

118
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:25,950
They are descriptive historical outcomes,
not a clean cohort of uniquely

119
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:31,060
published recommendations, and they are
not a forward-tested ROI claim.

120
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:35,210
We keep that limitation visible because a
record should be something

121
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:38,570
you can audit—not a number you are asked
to accept on

122
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:43,930
faith. For a stricter standard, Propeller
also maintains a forward record

123
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:46,000
for eligible featured public picks.

124
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:50,630
Those rows require publication before a
verified event start,

125
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:54,620
an exact side and line, a named book and
price,

126
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:56,320
and an exact settlement.

127
00:07:56,880 --> 00:08:00,800
That is the standard needed to talk
responsibly about ROI.

128
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:04,440
Propeller will not remove uncertainty from
sports.

129
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:09,960
Late injuries, role changes, sparse
samples, bad source data,

130
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,240
and line movement can all change an
analysis.

131
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:15,650
The goal is not to hand off your decision
to AI.

132
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:18,360
It is to make your research clearer,

133
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:20,600
faster, and easier to challenge.

134
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:25,330
Start with the free Prop Analyzer at
PropellerPicks.com.

135
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:27,780
Read the line. Inspect the agents.

136
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:31,680
Use fantasy projections for the question
they actually answer.

137
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:33,520
And make your own decision.
